ganV(){return"Days after issue before a first reminder is suggested, and before an invoice falls due when no payment term was set."},
ganW(){return"Seconds a server waits for the answer to a signed message it sent to another server before it sends the same message again. At least 30; keep it below the status lifetime."},
ganX(){return"Hours a server keeps the receipts of signed messages between servers, and a personal home the tombstones of ended memberships, before the hourly cleanup removes them. Never shorter than the longest status lifetime plus twice the clock difference."},
ganY(){return"Seconds of clock difference between the personal home and a workspace server that are still accepted, 0 to 30."},
ganZ(){return"Seconds a workspace server may rely on one identity status signed by the personal home. At most 900: a suspended account is refused new requests within this time plus the clock skew."},
gao_(){return"Seconds between two refreshes of the identity statuses a workspace server holds. Keep it below the status lifetime."},
gao0(){return"Fixed by the platform: the longest period one capacity figure may cover. It bounds the query."},
gao1(){return"Fixed by the platform: the months beyond the first that one finance figure may span (23 means 24 months in all). It bounds the query."},
gao2(){return"Where a new workspace starts when the device's region is unknown. A suggestion only; it decides no tax or issuer country."},
gao3(){return"What amounts are shown in before a workspace is connected, and where a new workspace starts. It never stands in for a missing invoice currency."},
gao4(){return"The format used before a member or workspace has chosen one. A member's own choice always wins."},
gao5(){return"The day weeks start on in calendars where a member chose none: the format's own, or always Monday, Sunday or Saturday. A member's own choice always wins."},
gao6(){return"Minutes the person has to confirm an action an assistant asked for. Requests already made keep their time. Can only be shortened."},
gao7(){return"Days a read operator notice is kept before it is purged. Unread notices, grants, consents and the audit trail are never purged by this value."},
gao8(){return"Minutes a successful check of the assistant endpoint counts before the interface is turned on. Can only be shortened."},
gao9(){return"Fixed by the platform: the longest window one assistant read may ask for. It bounds the query; it is not a permission to scan more."},
gaoa(){return"Minutes after sending in which the author may still correct a message. A workspace message reads its workspace, a personal or group message the platform value."},
gaob(){return"How many groups one person may create per hour. Can only be lowered."},
gaoc(){return"How many conversations the personal home and each workspace server return per page of the inbox; older ones come with Show older conversations."},
gaod(){return"Seconds between two refreshes of the inbox and its unread badge. Lower values load the server more."},
gaoe(){return"Seconds between two checks, by one device, for requests whose deadline has passed. Such a request shows as timed out at most this much later. 0 checks before every read of the inbox."},
gaof(){return"How many message requests one person may send per day to people who have not allowed them. Can only be lowered."},
gaog(){return"Seconds between two refreshes of an open conversation. Lower values load the server more."},
gaoh(){return"How many workspaces, people or groups the new discussion lists at a time; the next ones come with Show more."},
gaoi(){return"The longest text the new-discussion directory searches for. A longer search is refused, never cut."},
gaoj(){return"How many servers the personal space asks at once when it gathers your own records. A bound on the device's parallel reads, not on any server."},
gaok(){return"Seconds the personal space waits for one server's answer before it shows that server as unavailable and goes on with the others."},
gaol(){return"Fixed by the platform: the longest period one read of your reservations may ask for. It bounds the query."},
gaom(){return"How many of your reservations one server returns per page; the next page comes with Show more."},
gaon(){return"Days the personal space shows by default when it lists your reservations. You may choose another period, up to the ceiling."},
gaoo(){return"Minutes after its last sign of life that a person still counts as online. Keep it above the 2-minute heartbeat."},
gaop(){return"Minutes the app must have been out of sight (in the background, a hidden tab, a sleeping kiosk) before it re-reads everything it shows when it comes back. Switching windows never re-reads; a lost live connection always does."},
gaoq(){return"true: a member can export and erase their own data from the app. false: they file a rights request, which the personal data admin handles. Owners and the personal data admin are never blocked, and filing a request is always open."},
gaor(){return"average: every approved purchase of the item up to the end of the period, weighed by its units. last: the latest purchase dated by then. It changes no document, only the margin figures."},
gaos(){return"A payment of at least this amount cannot be recorded by the person who approved the bill it pays. 0 switches the rule off."},
gaot(){return"Bills of the space's supplier below this amount may be approved by the person who drafted or sent them, if that person may approve expenses. 0 keeps the rule that another person approves every bill. Rejecting always takes another person."},
gaou(){return"The most supplier lookups one person may make per minute on this server. Over the limit nothing is sent to the registry and the lookup is answered as busy."},
gaov(){return"How long the server waits for the company registry (VIES) before a supplier lookup counts as timed out. The person keeps what they typed and may retry or go on by hand."},
gaow(){return"Days an export the app recorded still counts as recent evidence that recovery works. Older than this, recovery reads as unverified."},
gaox(){return"For a Canadian business: the reference of the CRA authorisation (ETA s.286, ITA s.230) when its records are kept outside Canada. Empty means none is recorded."},
gaoy(){return"Two letters (ISO 3166), e.g. CA or DE, as your hosting contract states where the database and its backups are. Empty means not declared: the app then states no location."},
gaoz(){return"report or remove. What the nightly maintenance does with an uploaded invoice PDF that no recorded original names, a day after its upload: report names it in the maintenance record and removes nothing; remove deletes it, which cannot be undone."},
